the site allocations plan is a list of  predominantly housing sites that would  come forward if we were unable to  deliver a five-year housing land supply  as required by the core strategy we're  not in that position we have a really  strong five-year housing land supply and  that's evidenced by the fact that within  the last three months a developer  brought forward an appeal based on  challenging a five-year housing land  supply when they saw our numbers they  abandoned the appeal so that's a really  strong place to start with secondly we  have a set of allocated sites already in  the core strategy which were on track  for delivery and as long as those sites  are delivered there is no need for us to  consider any of the reserve sites the  third area where sites could come  forward would be into what's called a  duty to cooperate in short if Birmingham  and Coventry can't demonstrate they've  got sufficient land to meet their needs  as a neighboring Authority we have to  help out the good news is we'd already  factored in a number of houses and have  delivered a number of houses to meet  that anticipated need so we're a really  long way from ever having to be in that  position and if anybody tried to bring a  site forward they would have to  demonstrate that firstly Birmingham or  Coventry had asked for and requested us  to cooperate and that there was no other  mechanism to deliver those houses within  the core strategy as it currently stands  so the bar is set really high in terms  of bringing any of those sites on stream  site allocations plan identifies a 20%  buffer which is circa 3,000 homes as I  said earlier on this is a reserve list  the bar is set extremely high and  there's a mechanism to ensure that when  people try to bring these sites forward  they have to hit certain checkmarks  around the five year land supply duty to  cooperate and we are nowhere near that  so I am absolutely confident there are  nearly five hundred homes in my own Ward  in biddeford identified in this plan and  I'm completely satisfied that the sites  are very unlikely ever to come forward  within this core strategy period I'd  like to send a message out to land  owners to property developers and also  to our local communities this reserve  listings exactly what it says it's a  reserve list  there is no need for us to bring these  sights forward as long as we deliver the  sights that are already allocated so if  you're a landowner if you're a developer  don't waste your time don't waste your  money and don't waste the effort of this  councils officers in bringing sites  forward which have no prospect  whatsoever of coming forward as  development sites within the core  strategy period up to twenty thirty one  I would also add that we are obliged to  undertake a review the core strategy  which will happen in 2020 that core  strategy review will undoubtedly look to  change the shape of future development  and will ultimately lead post 2031 to a  new core strategy so although we have to  go through this exercise this set of  sites could well be redundant early into  next year
 

